    "traits": {
      "value": [
        {
          "resource_id": "monster_trait",
          "stats": {
            "trait_name": {
              "value": "Eternal Damnation"
            },
            "trait_description": {
              "value": "(divine, necromancy)\n\nAs long as its _soul chain_ remains intact, a forge-spurned can't be truly destroyed. It rises again fully healed at the next sundown, even if its physical body was destroyed."
            },
            "id": "11630001-5cfe-4b2e-aa4c-c1a158d581ce",
            "updated_at": {
              "value": "2026-03-19T22:58:45.024646"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "resource_id": "monster_trait",
          "stats": {
            "trait_name": {
              "value": "Searing Heat"
            },
            "trait_description": {
              "value": "(fire)\n\nA creature that touches a forge-spurned (including by grappling it or hitting it with an unarmed attack) takes 2d6 fire damage with a 21 basic Reflex save."
            },
            "id": "b2e6eea2-7e7d-4532-94b2-0f5874ceba63",
            "updated_at": {
              "value": "2026-03-19T22:58:45.024646"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "resource_id": "monster_trait",
          "stats": {
            "trait_name": {
              "value": "Soul Chain"
            },
            "trait_description": {
              "value": "(divine, fire, necromancy)\n\nIf a creature is slain by an attack from the _soul chain_ and the forge-spurned is able to retain the creature's corpse, it can bind the creature's soul into the _soul chain_ (as bind soul) with a day of work at a forge and a successful 20 Crafting check. An individual whose soul is bound in this way can't be resurrected unless the _soul chain_ is destroyed (Hardness 5, HP 20, BT 10)."
            },
            "id": "fad133d0-7d1c-4800-a775-62be668970ac",
            "updated_at": {
              "value": "2026-03-19T22:58:45.024646"
            }
          }
        }
